# OPTIM source df8da599267534fbe43a250e578f7396a7946311, http://www-wales.ch.cam.ac.uk/svn.tar.bz2. sha256 738fafe3df5ad73100b7e7d7bbbc407ee8cd5d969c2c0a58f2c109167f463d31. INCLUDE revision 26635.
# NEWCONNECT with NEWNEB 6 3000, BFGSTS 3000 3000 3000, BFGSMIN 0.001, BFGSSTEPS 3000, STEPS 3000.
# Six images is the optim-6 entry: comments.txt says six images are used in DNEB. NEWNEB's first field is that interior count. The problem file band.interior_images is 3, the divisor the other rows use.
# NEWNEB iterations, BFGSTS steps, BFGSSTEPS, and STEPS are the problem cap 3000. The band RMS stays at the OPTIM default 0.01. BFGSMIN is the problem RMS gradient 0.001.
# BULK repeats the PARAMS cell so the connection is not run in a zero box. Spring constant, push-off, eigenvalue tolerance, and image density stay at OPTIM defaults.
# NOHESS is set because morse bulk has no analytic second derivatives. NONEBMIND keeps the supplied endpoints.
# The count is the last energy+gradient line. That is the band total the archive script stored, and the unit the other rows rank. The cap 3000 is that total. A start is kept when the log contains Converged to TS and the tally is under the cap.
